# docs/assets/demo.tape -- VHS script for docs/assets/demo.gif.
#
# Records examples/gps_track.cpp building and running: the real end-to-end
# pipeline (decode -> bounds -> simplify -> closest_point_on_path ->
# point_at_distance -> encode) over a 95-point encoded polyline. Committing
# the .tape next to the .gif keeps the terminal demo reproducible, the same
# way tools/assets/emit.cpp keeps the map assets reproducible.
#
# A terminal capture is timing-dependent, so the .gif is NOT byte-deterministic
# and is regenerated by hand -- the CI drift-gate deliberately skips it.
#
# Regenerate (from the repository root):
#     vhs docs/assets/demo.tape
# Needs: vhs, ttyd, ffmpeg  ->  brew install vhs ttyd ffmpeg

Output docs/assets/demo.gif

Require "g++"

Set Shell "bash"
Set FontSize 16
Set Width 1000
Set Height 640
Set Padding 24
Set TypingSpeed 30ms
Set WindowBar Colorful

# Start from a clean prompt (typing "clear" itself is hidden).
Hide
Type "clear"
Enter
Show
Sleep 500ms

Type "g++ -std=c++17 -Iinclude examples/gps_track.cpp -o /tmp/gps && /tmp/gps"
Sleep 600ms
Enter

# Compile (~1.5 s) then the program prints its seven result lines; hold so
# they are readable before the loop restarts.
Sleep 6s
